#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:266
msgid ""
"Indices **MAY** choose to use the human-readable equivalents suggested above "
"in their UI elements, if appropriate. Alternatively, indices **MAY** choose "
"their own appropriate human-readable equivalents for UI elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:270
msgid ""
"Packagers and metadata producers **MAY** choose to use any label that "
"normalizes to these labels (or their aliases) to communicate specific URL "
"intents to package indices and downstreams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:274
msgid ""
"Similarly, indices **MAY** choose to specialize their rendering or "
"presentation of URLs with these labels, e.g. by presenting an appropriate "
"icon or tooltip for each label."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:278
msgid ""
"Indices **MAY** also specialize the rendering or presentation of additional "
"labels or URLs, including (but not limited to), labels that start with a "
"well-known label, and URLs that refer to a known service provider domain (e."
"g. for documentation hosting or issue tracking)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:283
msgid ""
"This PEP recognizes that the list of well-known labels is unlikely to remain "
"static, and that subsequent additions to it should not require the overhead "
"associated with a formal PEP process or new metadata version. As such, this "
"PEP proposes that the list above become a \"living\" list within the :ref:"
"`PyPA specifications <packaging:packaging-specifications>`."
