#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:290
msgid "Backwards Compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:293
msgid "Limited Impact"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:295
msgid ""
"This PEP is expected to have little to no impact on existing packaging "
"tooling or package indices:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:298
msgid ""
"Packaging tooling: no changes to the correctness or well-formedness of the "
"core metadata. This PEP proposes deprecations as well as behavioral "
"refinements, but all currently (and historically) produced metadata will "
"continue to be valid per the rules of its respective version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:302
msgid ""
"Package indices: indices will continue to expect well-formed core metadata, "
"with no behavioral changes. Indices **MAY** choose to emit warnings or "
"notifications on the presence of now-deprecated fields, :ref:`per above "
"<package-indices>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:310
msgid "Future Considerations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:312
msgid "This PEP does not stipulate or require any future metadata changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:314
msgid ""
"However, per :ref:`metadata-producers` and :ref:`conventions-for-labels`, we "
"identify the following potential future goals for a new major release of the "
"core metadata standards:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:318
msgid ""
"Outright removal of support for ``Home-page`` and ``Download-URL`` in the "
"next major core metadata version. If removed, package indices and consumers "
"**MUST** reject metadata containing these fields when said metadata is of "
"the new major version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:322
msgid ""
"Enforcement of label normalization. If enforced, package producers **MUST** "
"emit only normalized ``Project-URL`` labels when generating distribution "
"metadata, and package indices and consumers **MUST** reject distributions "
"containing non-normalized labels. Note: requiring normalization merely "
"restricts labels to lowercase text, and excludes whitespace and punctuation. "
"It does NOT restrict project URLs solely to the use of \"well-known\" labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:330
msgid ""
"These potential changes would be backwards incompatible, hence their "
"inclusion only in this section. Acceptance of this PEP does NOT commit any "
"future metadata revision to actually making these changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:335
msgid "Security Implications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:337
msgid ""
"This PEP does not identify any positive or negative security implications "
"associated with deprecating ``Home-page`` and ``Download-URL`` or with label "
"normalization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:342
msgid "How To Teach This"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:344
msgid ""
"The changes in this PEP should be transparent to the majority of the "
"packaging ecosystem's userbase; the primary beneficiaries of this PEP's "
"changes are packaging tooling authors and index maintainers, who will be "
"able to reduce the number of unique URL fields produced and checked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:349
msgid ""
"A small number of package maintainers may observe new warnings or "
"notifications from their index of choice, should the index choose to ignore "
"``Home-page`` and ``Download-URL`` as suggested. Similarly, a small number "
"of package maintainers may observe that their index of choice no longer "
"renders their URLs, if only present in the deprecated fields. However, no "
"package maintainers should observe rejected package uploads or other "
"breaking changes to packaging workflows due to this PEP's proposed changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:357
msgid ""
"Anybody who observes warnings or changes to the presentation of URLs on "
"indices can be taught about this PEP's behavior via official packaging "
"resources, such as the :ref:`Python Packaging User Guide <packaging>` and "
"`PyPI's user documentation <https://docs.pypi.org/>`__, the latter of which "
"already contains an informal description of PyPI's URL handling behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0753.rst:364
msgid ""
"If this PEP is accepted, the authors of this PEP will coordinate to update "
"and cross-link the resources mentioned above."
msgstr ""

